WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.780
(perky music)

00:00:04.949 --> 00:00:07.782
- Atropa belladonna will kill you.

00:00:10.158 --> 00:00:13.499
Datura will put you to sleep, forever.

00:00:13.499 --> 00:00:15.499
Aconitine will kill you.

00:00:16.506 --> 00:00:19.923
Laurel will produce cyanide and kill you.

00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.878
Every plant here in the
Poison Garden is poisonous

00:00:27.878 --> 00:00:30.545
and has the ability to kill you.

00:00:32.638 --> 00:00:35.070
My name's Trevor Jones
and I'm the head gardener

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:36.320
of Alnwick Garden.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.400
This plant is giant hogweed.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.862
It will get up to around
about eight foot high.

00:00:40.862 --> 00:00:43.230
It's phototoxic, so it will burn your skin

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.459
and give you blisters
for up to seven years.

00:00:46.459 --> 00:00:49.486
This garden is set in the
war garden of the old castle

00:00:49.486 --> 00:00:51.729
in Northumberland, U.K.

00:00:51.729 --> 00:00:54.420
We have around about 95 plants

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:57.118
and we're adding to the
collection all the time.

00:00:57.118 --> 00:00:59.748
This plant is aconitine, or monkshood.

00:00:59.748 --> 00:01:01.820
Wonderful blue flowers,
but the whole of the plant

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.129
is poisonous.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:06.278
The berries crushed up and
fed to you will kill you.

00:01:06.278 --> 00:01:08.557
The leaves themselves will kill you also,

00:01:08.557 --> 00:01:10.516
as will the root and the stem.

00:01:10.516 --> 00:01:11.988
We have to obviously maintain the garden,

00:01:11.988 --> 00:01:14.825
so we have to tend the
plants, and when we do that

00:01:14.825 --> 00:01:17.318
we have to be very careful
of the way we operate,

00:01:17.318 --> 00:01:19.618
so we have to cover some of our skin

00:01:19.618 --> 00:01:23.388
when we deal with
particularly dangerous plants.

00:01:23.388 --> 00:01:24.809
This plant is laurel.

00:01:24.809 --> 00:01:28.350
It produces cyanide, and we all
know what that'll do to you.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:30.055
So it was the brainchild of the duchess,

00:01:30.055 --> 00:01:31.453
the Duchess of Northumberland,

00:01:31.453 --> 00:01:33.407
so rather than having a herb garden,

00:01:33.407 --> 00:01:35.406
she decided to create more interest

00:01:35.406 --> 00:01:36.796
and have a poison garden.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.304
They're very very common plants.

00:01:38.304 --> 00:01:39.868
In fact, a lot of them are what we call

00:01:39.868 --> 00:01:41.658
cottage garden plants, and they're grown

00:01:41.658 --> 00:01:43.756
in many people's gardens,
but people don't know

00:01:43.756 --> 00:01:46.256
how harmful they actually are.

00:01:47.407 --> 00:01:49.108
This is atropa belladonna.

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:52.396
Four berries are enough to kill a child.

00:01:52.396 --> 00:01:54.628
People are intrigued by poisonous plants.

00:01:54.628 --> 00:01:56.148
I'm often very worried when they come out

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:58.565
because many of them will be
growing these plants at home,

00:01:58.565 --> 00:02:00.330
and they don't realize the powerful impact

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:02.997
plants can have on us as humans.

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:06.482
- Definitely.

00:02:07.643 --> 00:02:11.810
- It's a good way to get
rid of your wife. (chuckles)

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.614
I don't know.

00:02:13.614 --> 00:02:15.864
(laughter)

